# Line endings, settled here rather than left to each contributor's git config.
#
# Two things in this repository are compared byte for byte: the golden format fixtures, and the
# generated error-code table. A checkout that rewrites line endings breaks both — on Windows the
# table failed its own drift check while every line matched, which is what a CRLF conversion
# looks like, and a converted binary fixture would be silent corruption of the thing that exists
# to detect corruption.

# Text is LF everywhere, in the working tree as well as the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact fixtures. `binary` means "never convert, never diff as text".
testdata/** binary
# Fuzz corpus entries are raw bytes that must reach the decoder unaltered — a converted
# newline inside one is a regression case that silently stops reproducing its crash.
crates/*/fuzz/corpus/** binary
*.wasm binary
*.node binary
*.a binary
*.dylib binary
*.so binary
*.dll binary
*.png binary

# Scripts must keep LF even on Windows, or the shebang line carries a stray carriage return and
# the interpreter is not found.
*.sh text eol=lf
